rule: TEST_PATCHES_SUBJECT
title: a test patches its subject through an f-string target built from a module constant
origin: #196 188.5 C - f"{MODULE}.invoice_total" is read one hop: each part a string literal or a name bound once to one
=== before: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import billing


def test_invoice_total(mocker):
    items = [10.0, 90.0]
    assert billing.invoice_total(items, 0.053) == 105.3
=== after: tests/test_billing.py ===
from app import billing

MODULE = "app.billing"


def test_invoice_total(mocker):
    mocker.patch(f"{MODULE}.invoice_total", return_value=105.3)
    items = [10.0, 90.0]
    assert billing.invoice_total(items, 0.053) == 105.3
=== head: src/app/billing.py ===
def invoice_total(items, tax):
    return round(sum(items) * (1 + tax), 2)
